# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GlassBox environment. Copy to `.env` and fill in.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# EVERY VALUE HERE IS OPTIONAL. The engine runs complete without any of them:
#
#     python run.py
#
# ...needs no key, no network and no model download. That is deliberate -- the
# judges will run this on a machine we have never seen, so the core path cannot
# depend on a secret being present.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- NVIDIA NIM (optional enrichment layer) --------------------------------
# Powers the model-proposal layer, which fills attribute slots the text does
# not contain -- e.g. it knows a Frigidaire PDSH4816AF runs at 120 V, which is
# nowhere in that row's description. Proposals are validated against each
# slot's controlled vocabulary, labelled as proposals rather than facts, scored
# at 0.50 confidence against 0.95 for a text extraction, and always routed to
# human review.
#
# Get a key: https://build.nvidia.com  ->  sign in  ->  any model page  ->
#            "Get API Key". Free credits, no card required.
# The key looks like: nvapi-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#
# WHERE IT GOES:
#   * local runs        -> this file, as `.env` (never commit it; .gitignore
#                          already excludes `.env`)
#   * Hugging Face Space-> Settings > Variables and secrets > New secret,
#                          name NVIDIA_API_KEY. Do NOT paste it into app.py.
NVIDIA_API_KEY=

# Then enable it explicitly -- it never turns itself on:
#     python run.py --propose
# ...or flip "Model proposals" in the app sidebar (the toggle stays disabled
# until a key is present).

# --- optional overrides ----------------------------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible endpoint works; NVIDIA NIM is just the default.
# GLASSBOX_LLM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
# GLASSBOX_LLM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.3-70b-instruct

# Hard ceiling on model calls per run, so a full-catalogue run cannot
# accidentally burn a quota. Responses are cached to disk, so a rerun over the
# same rows costs nothing.
# GLASSBOX_LLM_MAX_CALLS=250
# GLASSBOX_LLM_CACHE=outputs/llm_cache.jsonl
